> ## Guffin Sampling/Cache Logic Change Checklist

**Goal:** Ensure correctness and performance without breaking existing functionality.

**I. Design & Planning (Before Coding)**

*   [ ] **Problem Definition:** Clearly define the problem being solved and expected performance gain.
*   [ ] **Architecture Impact:** Identify which modules (Session, Plans, Target, Sampler) are affected.
*   [ ] **Ownership & Lifecycle:** Document any changes to data ownership, lifetime, or residency.
*   [ ] **Numerical Assumptions:** Explicitly state any assumptions about precision or numerical stability.

**II. Automated Correctness Checks (Mandatory)**

*   [ ] **Lossless Sampling:** Add/update `lossless_sampling_tests.cpp` to verify probability distribution preservation.
*   [ ] **Numerical Validation:** Implement/update `gemma3_metal_tests.cpp` for packed projections & fused sum accuracy.
*   [ ] **Runtime Logic:** Create/update `gemma3_target_runtime_tests.cpp` to test core inference logic and callbacks.
*   [ ] **Tensor Validation:** Ensure `tensor_tests.cpp` covers any new or modified tensor operations.
*   [ ] **Code Review:** Submit changes for thorough code review focusing on ownership and potential numerical issues.

**III. Performance Measurements (Post-Correctness Checks)**

*   [ ] **Baseline Capture:** Record existing performance metrics (tokens/s, TTFT) on representative prompts.
*   [ ] **Real-World Chat:** Measure performance with *actual* chat sessions (not just synthetic benchmarks).
*   [ ] **Variance Analysis:** Ensure observed improvements are statistically significant, not just noise.
*   [ ] **Documentation:** Record changes, rationale, and measured results in `PERFORMANCE.md`.



**Note:** Changes must align with `ENGINE_PRINCIPLES.md`—favor removing work over micro-optimizations.
